## Change

- Added `MessageExtSubtype` hooks for Java `MessageClientExt.getOffsetMsgId()`
  and `setOffsetMsgId(String)`. The owned getter result supports custom
  subtypes backed by interior mutable state.
- Routed Rust `MessageClientExt` get/set methods through the retained subtype.
  `getMsgId()` continues to prefer the live `UNIQ_KEY` property, then reaches
  the virtual offset getter. Base `setMsgId` remains a no-op unless the
  runtime subtype overrides it.
- Added two invoked Java direct-consume cases for an offset-only subclass,
  both without and with `UNIQ_KEY`. Rust also tests wrapper setter dispatch,
  unique-ID precedence/live changes, and conversion to `MessageExt`.

